writeFile [SimTalk] - JSON
Writes the JSON source code from the specified JSON variable to the specified text file.
Type
Method
Syntax
<json_Variable>.writeFile(FileName:string) → void
Parameter
The parameter FileName of data type string designates the path to and the name of the text file to which
the source code is going to be written.
Return Value
The return value is void.
Example
-- our text file JSON.txt contains this JSON source code:
{
  "first_name": "John",
  "last_name": "Doe",
  "age": 46,
  "address": {
    "street_address": "42 42nd Street",
    "city": "New York",
    "state": "NY",
    "postal_code": "10021-3100"
  }
}
